# Next.js Project Rules

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router, latest version)
- **Language**: JavaScript (ES6+, no TypeScript)
- **Styling**: Styled Components (CSS-in-JS)
- **Data**: No database — content comes from constants and locale JSON files
- **Theme**: Themed styled components with dark/light mode support
- **Responsive**: Mobile-first, fully responsive design

## Rule Files
This project uses modular rule files organized by concern:
- `project-structure.mdc` - Directory organization and file structure
- `components.mdc` - Component structure and reusable components
- `styled-components.mdc` - Styled Components rules and patterns
- `nextjs.mdc` - Next.js App Router specific rules
- `code-style.mdc` - JavaScript style, naming conventions, imports
- `constants.mdc` - Constants and configuration rules
- `performance.mdc` - Performance optimization rules
- `responsive.mdc` - Responsive design rules
- `theme.mdc` - Theme and styling rules
- `api-routes.mdc` - API routes rules
- `security.mdc` - Security rules
- `accessibility.mdc` - Accessibility rules
- `quality.mdc` - Testing and code quality
- `reusability.mdc` - Reusability and uniformity standards

## Reproducibility Standards
- **Code Templates**: Use the templates in `components.mdc` and `styled-components.mdc`
- **Naming Conventions**: Follow strict naming conventions (see `reusability.mdc`)
- **Import Order**: Follow strict import order (see `project-structure.mdc`)
- **Theme Usage**: Always use theme variables, never hardcode values
- **Error Handling**: All async operations must use try/catch
- **Documentation**: All components/functions must have JSDoc comments
